# Line endings are the repository's business only where something outside it
# cares. Exactly two things do.
#
# cmd.exe is the first.
*.cmd text eol=crlf

# The second is an expectation: `test/e2e/run` and `examples/run` compare one of
# these byte for byte with what a program printed, and `echo` writes a newline
# and never a carriage return. A checkout that turned these into CRLF would fail
# every comparison on a program that is right.
*.expected text eol=lf

# Everything else is text with the endings it was written with, and these are
# not text at all — a workbook and a spreadsheet. No binary is tracked besides
# the ones an example reads.
*.xlsx binary
*.ods binary
